### Preserve manual UI-test module selection

**Severity:** `high`

The new exact comparison is correct for automatically resolved project names, but this template is also used by manually selected UI-test runs. Those runs may pass a project name whose runtime configuration uses a different assembly name, such as `MouseUtils.UITests` and `PowerToys.MouseUtils.UITests.runtimeconfig.json`; the exact check then selects no runner and fails the job. Keep exact matching for automatic selection while retaining the established partial match for manual values.

```suggestion
        $entries = $entries | Where-Object {
          $projectName = $_.Name -replace '\.runtimeconfig\.json$', ''
          if (-not [string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($env:AUTO_UI_TEST_MODULES)) {
            $modules -contains $projectName
          } else {
            @($modules | Where-Object { $projectName -like "*$_*" }).Count -gt 0
          }
        }
```
